\\ arith.6502 - the race logic's 16-bit signed arithmetic, as the ST's 68000 does it (D9): a product's low
\\ word kept (muls.w, then move.w), a quotient rounded towards 0 (divs.w). Both take and give their number in
\\ num, so one's result is the next's input.

ZA_AUTO2 num                            ; mul_s16's and div_s16's number, in and out

\\ A signed 16-bit number times a small signed one: the product's low 16 bits.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\     A: the multiplier, -127 to 127, the flags set by it (its sign is read from N)
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the product's low 16 bits
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.mul_s16
{
    ZA_AUTO2 acc                        ; local: the sum
    ZA_AUTO1 m                          ; local: the multiplier's bits left
    ZA_AUTO1 neg                        ; local: bit 7, the multiplier's sign

    STA neg
    BPL @+
    EOR #&FF:INC A                      ; |multiplier|
.@
    STA m
    STZ acc:STZ acc+1
.bit
    LSR m
    BCC shift
    CLC
    LDA acc:ADC num:STA acc
    LDA acc+1:ADC num+1:STA acc+1
.shift
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    LDA m:BNE bit

    BIT neg:BMI negate
    LDA acc:STA num
    LDA acc+1:STA num+1
    RTS
.negate
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC acc:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC acc+1:STA num+1
    RTS
}

\\ A signed 16-bit number divided by a positive one, the quotient rounded towards 0 (divs.w's). The
\\ quotient always fits: the divisor is at least 1 and the number at most 32,768 from 0.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\     A: the divisor, 1 to 127
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the quotient
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.div_s16
{
    ZA_AUTO1 d                          ; local: the divisor
    ZA_AUTO1 neg                        ; local: bit 7, the number's sign

    STA d
    LDA num:ORA num+1:BNE some
    RTS                                 ; 0: 0
.some
    LDA num+1:STA neg
    BPL @+
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC num:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC num+1:STA num+1
.@
    LDA num+1:CMP d:BCS long

    \\ the high byte under the divisor: the quotient fits a byte, and the high byte is the remainder so far,
    \\ so 8 steps on the low byte do (the remainder stays under d, at most 127: no carry out). Each step's
    \\ quotient bit is its C, shifted in by the next step's ROL, the last by one more (the C the first shifts
    \\ in comes out of that one: never in the quotient or the remainder)

    FOR i = 1..8
        ROL num
        ROL A
        CMP d:BCC @+
        SBC d                           ; (C set: stays set)
    .@
    NEXT
    ROL num
    STZ num+1
    BRA sign

    \\ else all 16 steps, the same way
.long
    LDA #0
    LDY #16
.bit
    ROL num:ROL num+1
    ROL A
    CMP d:BCC @+
    SBC d                               ; (C set: stays set)
.@
    DEY
    BNE bit
    ROL num:ROL num+1

.sign
    BIT neg:BPL @+
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC num:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC num+1:STA num+1
.@
    RTS
}

\\ num divided by 8, rounded towards 0: three shifts when it's positive (a position nearly always is).
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the quotient
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.div8_s16
{
    LDA num+1:BMI negative
    LSR A:ROR num
    LSR A:ROR num
    LSR A:ROR num
    STA num+1
    RTS
.negative
    LDA #8:JMP div_s16
}

\\ num times a direction vector's step, the product's low 16 bits, as mul_s16 but only for the steps DirX and
\\ DirY hold (0, 3, 6, 7, 8 and their negatives), by shifts and adds.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\     A: the step, the flags set by it (its sign is read from N)
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the product's low 16 bits
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.mul_dir
{
    ZA_AUTO2 n                          ; local: the number, or twice it
    ZA_AUTO1 neg                        ; local: bit 7, the step's sign

    STA neg
    BPL @+
    EOR #&FF:INC A
.@
    TAY
    LDA num:STA n
    LDA num+1:STA n+1
    CPY #8:BEQ x8
    CPY #7:BEQ x7
    CPY #6:BEQ x6
    CPY #3:BEQ x3
    STZ num:STZ num+1                   ; 0
    RTS
.x3                                     ; 2n + n
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    BRA addn
.x6                                     ; 4n + 2n
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    LDA num:STA n
    LDA num+1:STA n+1
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    BRA addn
.x7                                     ; 8n - n
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    SEC
    LDA num:SBC n:STA num
    LDA num+1:SBC n+1:STA num+1
    BRA sign
.x8
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    BRA sign
.addn
    CLC
    LDA num:ADC n:STA num
    LDA num+1:ADC n+1:STA num+1
.sign
    BIT neg:BPL @+
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC num:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC num+1:STA num+1
.@
    RTS
}
